From cbfd20667f5bd9b4d0279d4137e8c7c75d00ccba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stacc <jarettrsdunn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:49:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Seed openzoo at first launch: root bootstrap, localhost x402
 proxy, omarchymax one-liner, ChatGPT desktop provider

The locked package set is untouched: packages.txt and the package lock
stay exactly what the build verified. Node and the openzoo CLI are
instead installed by a root oneshot (try-omarchy-openzoo-bootstrap.service
-> /usr/local/lib/try-omarchy/openzoo-bootstrap) on the first ONLINE boot
via `pacman -Sy nodejs npm` and `npm i -g openzoo`. The only state is the
stamp /var/lib/try-omarchy/openzoo-bootstrapped; a boot without network
leaves no stamp and the unit simply retries on the next boot.

Every user session runs a localhost-only x402 pay-per-call proxy on :8402
(openzoo-proxy.service, `openzoo proxy` with OPENZOO_NO_TUNNEL=1, wanted
by default.target). It waits for the bootstrap rather than failing before
the CLI exists, and never opens a public tunnel that could spend the
wallet unattended.

The first graphical login runs `curl -fsSL openzoo.fun/omarchymax | bash`
once (openzoo-first-launch.service, a user oneshot wanted by
graphical-session.target, conditioned on !%h/.openzoo/omarchymax-done):
the agent in Omarchy's agent list, the bar widget, local ingest, and the
ChatGPT desktop seed. A login without network leaves no stamp and retries
at the next login.

/etc/skel seeds ~/.codex/config.toml with model_provider = "openzoo"
pointing at http://localhost:8402/v1, and environment.d exports the
OPENZOO_API_KEY the provider names, so the Codex side of OpenAI's ChatGPT
desktop app pays per turn through the proxy with no OpenAI account.
`try-omarchy-chatgpt --deb <file|url>` unpacks the proprietary amd64
.deb (not shipped; the user downloads it from https://chatgpt.com/download)
under ~/.openzoo/apps/chatgpt and launches it.

The new units, wants symlinks, scripts, skel config, and environment.d
conf are added to the compat overlay (compat_revision 12 -> 13) so
persistent disks from earlier releases receive them too.

New tests in guest/tests/test_openzoo.py pin the units, the symlinks, the
seeded provider, the absence of nodejs/npm from packages.txt, and that
the ChatGPT wrapper bakes in no .deb URL; guest/tests/verify.py gains the
same checks and the revision pin.

